      "post_date": "Mon Sep 28, 2009 1:32 pm",
      "post_datetime": "2009-09-28T18:32:00+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Mask",
      "content_md": "Thank you all. It has been (and still is) a long hard road and not without the help of some really great people. I think getting to talk to people with the same passion is as equally rewarding as the hologram itself. As Joesph Campbell would say, finding one's bliss.\n\nDave correct as always my friend.\n\nI have a really hard time devoting the time needed to set up the piece as well as finding a interesting enough subjects. I know that the plate should be larger than the subject but I only had 4x5 plates and an object nearly that big so I got stuck.\n\nI also still get some background haze reflected from the black felt.\n\nSome greenies still pop up too from time to time.\n\nI'll get there one day",
      "signature": "",
      "attachments": [],
      "quotes": [],
      "is_first_post": false,
      "url": "https://holographyforum.org/forum/viewtopic.php?p=63889#p63889"
    },
